# Implementation Plan — Phase 1: Auto-tagging & Summarization

Implement document text extraction (PDF & Plaintext), wire the Claude AI pipeline task to auto-generate summaries, tag chips, and suggested folders, and surface live AI insights inside the Google Drive UI preview modal and Django admin.

---

## Proposed Changes

### 1 — Text Extractors (`ai_features/extractors/`)

#### [NEW] `ai_features/extractors/__init__.py`
#### [NEW] `ai_features/extractors/base.py`

- Dispatcher `extract_text(file_path: str, extension: str) -> str | None`: routes files to appropriate extractor by extension.

#### [NEW] `ai_features/extractors/pdf.py`

- Uses `pdfplumber` to extract clean page text from `.pdf` files.

#### [NEW] `ai_features/extractors/plaintext.py`

- Reads `.txt`, `.md`, `.json`, `.py`, `.js`, `.html`, `.css`, `.csv`, `.xml` files with encoding detection (`utf-8`, `latin-1`).

---

### 2 — Background Analysis Pipeline (`ai_features/tasks.py`)

#### [MODIFY] [tasks.py](file:///c:/Programs/Python/skyvault/ai_features/tasks.py)

- `analyze_file(file_id: int)`:
  1. Retrieves `File` record and sets `FileAnalysis.status = PROCESSING`.
  2. Runs text extraction. If no text or unsupported format -> sets status `SKIPPED`.
  3. Sends text snippet (up to 8,000 characters) to Claude using `generate_json()`.
  4. Saves `summary`, `tags` (lowercase list), `suggested_folder`, and `extracted_text`, updating status to `DONE`.
  5. Catches any processing/API exceptions, updating status to `FAILED` with `error_message`.

---

